<GuideLayout
  title="Technical Performance: A Deep Dive into Fitclo’s Sculpting Fabrics vs. Industry Standards"
  type="FABRIC R&D"
  description="An engineering-focused analysis of Fitclo's high-compression fabrics, highlighting why professional brands choose our textiles for longevity and performance."
>
  <h2>Fabric is the Foundation</h2>
  <p>For established brands, quality consistency is the #1 priority. A single batch of "see-through" leggings can destroy years of brand reputation. At Fitclo, we approach fabric as an engineering challenge, not just a textile choice.</p>

  <img src="/images/migrated/third-party/hfacb2ef50051497481f5deeb487294f0j-8374e16cc4.webp" alt="Fitclo Fabric R&D: Technical Inspection of High-Compression Textiles" class="w-full rounded-2xl my-8 shadow-xl" />

  <h3>The "Sculpt" Factor: Compression vs. Comfort</h3>
  <p>Most manufacturers use standard polyester/spandex blends. Fitclo’s proprietary <strong>Sculpting Fabric</strong> uses a high-gauge Nylon 6,6 blend that offers superior compression without the restrictive "suffocating" feel of cheaper alternatives.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>High GSM (Grams per Square Meter):</strong> Ensures 100% squat-proof transparency.</li>
    <li><strong>Interlock Knit:</strong> Prevents "pilling" and maintains shape even after 500+ hours of wear.</li>
    <li><strong>Matte Luxury Finish:</strong> Engineered specifically for the "minimalist luxury" aesthetic preferred by high-end labels.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Seam Engineering for Professional Standards</h3>
  <p>A premium fabric deserves premium construction. We utilize <strong>4-Needle 6-Thread Flatlock</strong> stitching as our standard for performance wear. This creates a seam that is stronger than the fabric itself, eliminating the risk of bursting during high-intensity training.</p>

  <img src="/images/migrated/third-party/h88eedc1321c748f4a1a389688f71d995e-c6d8fdb3bc.webp" alt="Seam Detail: Professional 4-Needle 6-Thread Construction" class="w-full rounded-2xl my-8 shadow-xl" />

  <h3>Standardization for Global Markets</h3>
  <p>Our fabrics are <strong>OEKO-TEX Standard 100</strong> certified, ensuring they are free from harmful chemicals. For US and EU brands, this compliance isn't just a benefit—it's a requirement for entering professional retail environments.</p>
